{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זה יתנו כל העבר על", :translit "zeh yitenu kol ha'over al", :gloss "this they shall give, every one who passes over"} {:he "זה היה כמין מטבע של אש", :translit "zeh hayah kemin matbe'a shel esh", :gloss "this was like a coin of fire"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "זה יתנו כל העבר על", :b "זה היה כמין מטבע של אש"}], :frame {:text "The Midrash relates that when Moses descended from Mount Sinai and saw the golden calf, he declared: \"This is what they gave!\" — and God showed him a coin of fire descending from beneath the throne of glory, the heavenly prototype of the half-shekel each Israelite was to give (Exodus 30:13). The Midrash Tanchuma explains that the Holy One showed Moses a coin of fire weighing a half-shekel and said: 'Like this they shall give.'", :sources ["Midrash Tanchuma Ki Tisa 9" "Shemot Rabbah 41:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "זה יתנו", :translit "zeh yitenu", :gloss "this they shall give"} {:he "ז\"ה", :translit "z\"h", :gloss "abbreviation for the twelve tribes"} {:he "עשרים", :translit "esrim", :gloss "twenty"} {:he "עשיר ודל", :translit "ashir vedal", :gloss "rich and poor"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "ז\"ה read as abbreviation for the twelve tribes"} {:kind :gematria, :a "עשרים", :b "עשיר ודל"}], :frame {:text "Exodus 30:15 states that in the half-shekel census 'the rich shall not give more and the poor shall not give less,' establishing full equality. The Talmud records a dispute as to whether the tribe of Levi participated in the half-shekel census; the view that Levi did not give is attributed in Midrashic sources to the position that Levi was counted separately.", :sources ["Exodus 30:15" "Talmud Bavli Bekhorot 51a" "Midrash Tanchuma Ki Tisa 9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שקל", :translit "shekel", :gloss "shekel"} {:he "נפש", :translit "nefesh", :gloss "soul"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "שקל", :b "נפש"}], :frame {:text "Exodus 30:12 states that each Israelite gives a ransom for his